docs/WORK-ORDERS-archive.md:129:- [x] **BW-09 (MERGED) — Verbose-title fix is a BANDAID (confirmed).** ROOT CAUSE: DR persists a RAW un-sanitized title = `opts.query.slice(0,100)` at creation (deepResearch.ts:57 → POST /conversations → sqlite.py:247, verbatim, mid-word cut). The auto-titler is IDEMPOTENT (title_service.py:144 `if get_title(cid): return`) so the clean SUMMARIZER title is SKIPPED — the verbose value is never repaired. The only "fix" is a render-time CSS `truncate` (HistoryView.tsx:238 / ProjectsView.tsx:103) — cosmetic mask; DeepReportView.tsx:287 renders the full query as <h1> unclamped. EVIDENCE: the 12 longest persisted titles are ALL deep_research, each exactly 100 chars cut mid-word; build/agent titles are short+clean (they go through the sanitizing titler). FIX (sanitize at SOURCE): (a) don't seed a title on DR create → let the sanitizing titler generate a clean clamped one, OR (b) run the query through `sanitize_title`/`fallback_title` (word-boundary, ~60-char) before persist, OR (c) treat the query title as PROVISIONAL + let the titler/report-title (W-10) overwrite it (relax the idempotent skip for provisional titles).
